    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87">

                <pb facs="0175" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1949v02/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB/8–3149: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Holmes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-08-31T13:00:00+01:00">August 31, 1949—1
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3478. Deptel 3047 August 24, 8 p. m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d87-f1"/> re Chinese
                    proposal introduce Sino-Soviet treaty questions in GA. Embassy officer had
                    informal discussion Dening<anchor n="2" xml:id="d87-f2"/> this matter. Dening
                    stated Foreign Office questioned what concrete results Chinese expected to flow
                    from such move. Debate in GA would not restore Chinese rights Manchuria.
                    Therefore Foreign Office did not agree to support or not to support Chinese
                    proposal. Dening, however, agreed debate GA would provide western powers with
                    opportunity for propaganda vs Soviet imperialism.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Holmes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d87-f1" n="1" xml:id="d87-f1-content">
                <p>It repeated telegram 436, <ref target="#pg147">p. 147</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d87-f2" n="2" xml:id="d87-f2-content">
                <p>Maberly E. Dening, British Assistant Under Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs
                    (Far East).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
